# Bootstrap (Claude + Cursor parity)

On sessions involving multiple projects or architecture decisions:

1. **Read** `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` and `~/.omc/wiki/index.md` before acting.
2. Follow all rules in `CLAUDE.md`.

## Wiki routing

Both `~/.omc/wiki/` and every `<repo>/.omc/wiki/` are symlinks into one canonical store,
`~/.mmm/` (see `~/mmm/README.md`). The paths above still work unchanged — read/write them
exactly as before.

| Scope | Path | Tool (Claude Code) | Tool (Cursor) |
|-------|------|---------------------|----------------|
| Cross-project | `~/.omc/wiki/` | `global-wiki` skill — Read/Write/Grep | `mmm_query`/`mmm_read`/`mmm_write` MCP tools, else plain file read/write |
| Project-local | `<repo>/.omc/wiki/` | OMC `wiki_*` MCP (oh-my-claudecode only — not part of mmm) | Same `mmm_*` MCP tools (paths under `projects/<key>/`), else plain file read/write |

`wiki_*` MCP is an **oh-my-claudecode** feature, sandboxed to the worktree, and Cursor doesn't
have it at all. In Cursor use mmm's own `mmm_*` MCP tools when they're listed, otherwise read and
edit `.omc/wiki/*.md` as plain files. Without OMC installed,
Claude Code falls back the same way.

`mmm` (on `PATH` once installed) is a plain shell tool, not editor-specific — `mmm query "<term>"`
(instant, no LLM) and `mmm status`/`mmm doctor` work identically from a Cursor terminal. `mmm init
<path>` is the one-time setup that links a project's wiki in; safe to re-run, does nothing if
already linked.

After nontrivial research, write findings to `~/.omc/wiki/` before ending the task — bite-sized,
one topic per page, update an existing page before creating a new one.

## Subagents

- Read-only exploration (lookups, searches): prefer `simple-search` or `explore` Task subagents.
- Subagents inherit ponytail rules (YAGNI, shortest diff).

## Project context

If the repo has a project `CLAUDE.md`, read it after this bootstrap.
